#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who was your grandmother? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "I don't think so. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who was your grandmother? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Perhaps. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I don't think so. " or "Perhaps. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2127"
msgid "What is your world called, my friend? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I don't think so. " or "Perhaps. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Earth. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I don't think so. " or "Perhaps. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Britannia. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I don't think so. " or "Perhaps. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "I cannot say. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Earth. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:21F8"
msgid "How curious. Your world is named after one of the elements. This Earth must be a dark place indeed, filled with death. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Britannia. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2276"
msgid "What an odd sounding name. But strangely enough, it sounds familiar. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I cannot say. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2310"
msgid "Of course. I understand, it's a trade secret. You wouldn't want just anyone travelling there. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I cannot say. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2376"
msgid "Now I believe you asked me, of all things, what an element is. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I cannot say. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:23E9"
msgid "The elements number four: Earth, Water, Air, and Fire. And each has a power intrinsic to it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I cannot say. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Tell me more of Earth. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I cannot say. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "What can you say of Water? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I cannot say. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "I wish to know about Air. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Must you treat me like a child? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2552"
msgid "While you are in my Enclave, I will treat you however I please. But in truth I seek only to give warning to those uninitiated in our ways. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What rituals and ceremonies? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2634"
msgid "These rituals are shown to Sorcerers only. I will not reveal them to an outsider. To do so is punishable by death. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is the Lord of Flame? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:272C"
msgid "The Lord of Flame is the Father of the Daemons. He is the charnel pit from which all Fire comes. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is the Lord of Flame? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Father of Daemons? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is a Disciple? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:283B"
msgid "A Disciple is a Sorcerer who has not been made an Acolyte. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who or what is the Master? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:296A"
msgid "Master Malchir is the leader of our Enclave, but do not bother him with idle questions. He is a busy man and does not take kindly to interruptions of his work. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You have dealings with Tenebrae? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2B17"
msgid "Of course, dullard. Do you think we have the time to grow our own food? Make our own clothing? Craft our own buildings? We give Tenebrae the sure knowledge that the Lord of Flame will remain bound and that the volcano will remain dormant. In return they free us from the necessity of handling our more basic needs. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You have dealings with Tenebrae? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "You extort from the Tenebraens. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You have dealings with Tenebrae? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What does the Master research? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2CAE"
msgid "That is not your business. And don't bother to ask him. He won't tell you and will most likely be angered by your interruption. And if he is angry, I will be angry. Do you take my meaning? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What does the Master research? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2D03"
msgid "Good. I'm glad that you do. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What does the Master research? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2DB1"
msgid "Well, then. Let me be more explicit. If you anger Malchir, it is my duty to see that the source of his irritation is removed. Forcibly if necessary. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Spellcraft? Tell me more of this. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2E69"
msgid "Spells are our means of releasing and controlling the power of Fire. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me more of Earth. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:2FB5"
msgid "Earth is useful to Fire. It forms the channels through which Fire flows and provides the fuel by which it burns. The Mountain King and Lord of Flame have almost no conflict of wills. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me more of Earth. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Tell me of the Mountain King? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What can you say of Water? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:30E8"
msgid "That element is anathema to Fire as the Lurker is the nemesis of the Lord of Flame. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What can you say of Water? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Tell me of the Lurker? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to know about Air. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3264"
msgid "What is there to know? Air is at the beck and call of both Pyros and despised Hydros, and all but ignored by Lithos. Stratos is as weak as the those who follow her. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to know about Air. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Who is Pyros? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to know about Air. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Hydros, who is that? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to know about Air. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Who would Lithos be? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I wish to know about Air. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Tell me more of Stratos. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Father of Daemons? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3387"
msgid "Yes. All Daemons owe allegiance to Pyros for they are born when a life is ended in flames. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You extort from the Tenebraens. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:34ED"
msgid "With that single statement you have proven your total lack of understanding of our position. Perhaps I should introduce you to our patron Titan personally. I am quite sure that the Lord of Flame could teach you our value. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:35C7"
msgid "Your perceptions are both insightful and correct. Perhaps you have what it takes to become a Sorcerer. Does this prospect intrigue you? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3669"
msgid "Excellent! I will personally see to your tutoring... that is after you perform one small service for me. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "And what might that be? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "I see. You need a lackey. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Wait. I only said I was intrigued. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Whatever you want, I'll do. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3790"
msgid "I see. You are one who is willing to be a kith brought to slaughter. The Fire does not burn in your heart as it does in mine. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3817"
msgid "Your lack of interest is echoed by mine. I don't really think you have what it takes to be one of us, anyway. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:38A9"
msgid "So you have said before. Have you reconsidered your decision not to assist me? Will you seek the knowledge I wish? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Shrewd bargaining on both sides. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "I am sorry, but I must decline. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me of the Mountain King? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3A1D"
msgid "Of course, how could one be born in Pagan and not know of the Earth Titan. His Necromancers attend to the dead and put them beneath the ground to become his servants. His dominion is over the land and death. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me of the Mountain King? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "What do you know of Necromancers? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me of the Lurker? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3BCC"
msgid "That foul entity long ago attempted to claim all the lands beneath her dark waters. She was thwarted by a Necromancer who became the first Tempest. Were it not for the Tempests, we Sorcerers would have no other choice than to release the Lord of Flame to do battle with her. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me of the Lurker? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "What can you say about Tempests? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who is Pyros? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3D11"
msgid "Pyros is the name of the Lord of Flame, Titan of Fire. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hydros, who is that? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3DD3"
msgid "That accursed name belongs to the Lurker, Titan of Water. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who would Lithos be? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3E95"
msgid "He is called the Mountain King and is the Titan of Earth. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me more of Stratos. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:3FB5"
msgid "She is the Titan of Air and is followed by the Order of Enlightment. A group of misguided mages, called Theurgists, led by a blind, old man. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me more of Stratos. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Order of Enlightment? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me more of Stratos. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "What do you know of Theurgists? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me more of Stratos. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "Tell me of this 'blind, old man.' "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "And what might that be? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:40FB"
msgid "I will tell you only once a deal has been struck. Fear not. I won't make you do something you will regret. Are you prepared to undertake my task? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I see. You need a lackey. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:423A"
msgid "I have no need of a lackey. The task I require to be fulfilled will take skill and guile. And if you think of yourself as a lackey, I have no need of you. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Wait. I only said I was intrigued. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:42F7"
msgid "Then stop wasting my time! When you wish to deal in earnest, you may return. Until that time, you are dismissed. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Whatever you want, I'll do. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:441B"
msgid "Your enthusiasm is encouraging, however, your blind acceptance does not give me much faith in your ability to accomplish the task I've set for you. Ah, well. Only one way to find out. Are you prepared to undertake my task? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you know of Necromancers? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:44F9"
msgid "They are the practitioners of the magic of death. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What can you say about Tempests? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:45E6"
msgid "Naught but that they provide a service to the people by keeping the storms that plague Pagan away from this island. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Order of Enlightment? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4699"
msgid "They style themselves as a religious order, following their Mystic Voice. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Order of Enlightment? "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "What is this Mystic Voice? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you know of Theurgists? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:47D3"
msgid "They practice healing arts and it is said that their leader can even bring the dead back to life. All in all, they are a coven of weak fools afraid to die for a cause. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Tell me of this 'blind, old man.' "
msgctxt "bark 041C:48F8"
msgid "Stellos is his name and some say he's lived forever. I must give credit to this rumor, for he was an old man when I was a boy, and he hasn't changed a bit as I've become a man. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes, I am prepared. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4A14"
msgid "Excellent. The pact has been made. You will now be my Disciple. I sense that you are one of the rare individuals who the Fire has chosen. The Fire gives you the Truename: Daemion. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes, I am prepared. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4ADF"
msgid "Hold tightly to that name. It is your strength and also your weakness. My Truename is Morduin. I give it to you so that you may learn Sorcery from me. Reveal it upon pain of death. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes, I am prepared. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4BB7"
msgid "The task you must perform is to gain the Truename of Bane. She is a deceptive and conniving wench. Do not be fooled by her apparent friendliness. It's a ruse. She is power hungry and ambitious. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes, I am prepared. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4CAD"
msgid "It is my belief that she seeks the death of the Master and myself in order to become the most powerful Sorcerer of Pagan. This is not a problem in and of itself. It is how she intends to go about it that causes the problem. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes, I am prepared. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4D99"
msgid "Were she to issue the Calling and challenge by the proper methods, I would surely defeat her, but knowing this, she intends to strike clandestinely. The factions that exist in the Enclave will war if this happens. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Yes, I am prepared. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4E6C"
msgid "The possibility of losing control of the Lord of Flame will vastly increase and should this catastrophe come to pass, Pagan will be doomed.*You must hurry. I know not when she will attack. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Let me think on it more. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:4EF3"
msgid "You will not! I will have my answer now. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Let me think on it more. "
msgctxt "ask 041C"
msgid "I cannot accept an unknown task. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Let me think on it more. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:5011"
msgid "Very well, but remember, I am not a patient man. Do not delay over long, or I may retract my offer. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Let me think on it more. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:5068"
msgid "Be swift. I grow weary of waiting upon your answer. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Let me think on it more. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:50DA"
msgid "This capricious behavior begins to anger me. I will not endure it any further. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I won't do your dirty work! "
msgctxt "bark 041C:517D"
msgid "Dolt! You will regret ever having come to our Enclave! Prepare yourself for death! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is this Mystic Voice? "
msgctxt "bark 041C:51E7"
msgid "It is the alias of Stratos. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I cannot accept an unknown task. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:52C7"
msgid "I can understand your qualms, but put them to rest. I only seek a specific piece of information. Will you aid me? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I am sorry, but I must decline. "
msgctxt "bark 041C:53DA"
msgid "Very well. Perhaps you will reconsider with time. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after ""
msgctxt "bark 041C:5490"
msgid "I can't understand you. What did you say? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after ""
msgctxt "bark 041C:55D2"
msgid "If it would not be too much to ask, Master, I would like to become your First Acolyte. I have experience in dealing with the duties involved, and I promise you will not find my abilities wanting. Will you accept me? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after ""
msgctxt "bark 041C:563A"
msgid "Thank you, Master! You won't regret this decision. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after ""
msgctxt "bark 041C:56BB"
msgid "I understand, Master. I won't take any more of your time. Whatever I have is, of course, yours to take. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after ""
msgctxt "bark 041C:5764"
msgid "I hope I am performing my duties to your satisfaction. But I will attempt to improve them further. I must go now to return to my studies. "
msgstr ""
